      <memberdef kind="function" id="classthemis_1_1ingestion_1_1_generic_api_connector_1a206b09dfa79428f0cedcb321d28304ff" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void themis::ingestion::GenericApiConnector::setOAuthConfig</definition>
        <argsstring>(const OAuthConfig &amp;config)</argsstring>
        <name>setOAuthConfig</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::ingestion::GenericApiConnector::setOAuthConfig</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="structthemis_1_1ingestion_1_1_o_auth_config" kindref="compound">OAuthConfig</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>config</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Configure OAuth 2.0 token refresh for this connector. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Set OAuth Config.</para>
<para>When set, the connector will automatically attempt a token refresh (RFC 6749 §6) upon receiving HTTP 401. The refreshed access token is cached inside the connector and used for all subsequent requests in the same ingestion run.</para>
<para><computeroutput>config.access_token</computeroutput> is used immediately as the Bearer token; if it is empty, the static <computeroutput>api_key</computeroutput> (set via <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1ingestion_1_1_generic_api_connector_1a946f8e76ba702722ce1ab9ee9d931c25" kindref="member">setApiKey()</ref></computeroutput> or <computeroutput>options["api_key"]</computeroutput>) is used instead until the first refresh.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>config</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>OAuth configuration including token endpoint, client credentials, and the refresh token.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">config</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input parameter.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Implements setOAuthConfig without additional internal calls. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
